---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Brand Name Search Guide in India | BRNDNUR Advisory LLP";
const description = "Learn how to conduct a preliminary trademark search on the Indian IP database. Understand phonetic checks, visual conflicts, and Section 9/11 screening.";
const canonical = "https://brndnur.com/resources/brand-name-search-guide/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPath="/resources/brand-name-search-guide/"
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <!-- Breadcrumb & Hero -->
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="bn-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <a href="/resources/">Resources</a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <span class="current">Brand Name Search Guide</span>
        </nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Clearance Guide</p>
        <h1>Brand Name Search: The Essential Clearance Guide.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Why searching the official Indian trademark registry before launching your brand saves thousands in legal fees, redesigns, and lost momentum.</p>
        
        <div class="hero-badges">
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg>
            <span>IP India Official Database</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
            <span>Section 9 & 11 Risk Appraisal</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            <span>Phonetic & Semantic Screening</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="actions" style="margin-top: 28px;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/brand-name-search/">Request Clearance Check &rarr;</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/resources/">Back to Resources</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Guide Content -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <article class="legal-prose" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
          <div class="advisory-notice" style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 32px;">
            <div class="advisory-notice-icon">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="advisory-notice-content">
              <h4>The Cost of Skipping Due Diligence</h4>
              <p>Government statutory filing fees are non-refundable. If an examiner rejects your mark under Section 11 due to a prior identical mark, your fees are forfeited and you must begin again with an entirely new brand identity.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2>1. The Myth of the Simple Google Search</h2>
          <p>Many founders believe that if a domain is available or a quick Google search yields no local competitors, their chosen name is safe. In reality, the Trade Marks Registry includes thousands of registered trademarks, pending applications, and regional business marks that may not maintain an active social media presence yet possess senior statutory rights.</p>

          <h2>2. The 4 Layers of Trademark Search</h2>
          <div class="bn-table-wrap">
            <table class="bn-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Search Layer</th>
                  <th>Methodology</th>
                  <th>Why It Matters</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>1. Wordmark Match</strong></td>
                  <td>Direct exact & prefix/suffix matching</td>
                  <td>Catches obvious direct name conflicts</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>2. Phonetic Search</strong></td>
                  <td>Sound-alike algorithms & variant spellings</td>
                  <td>Blocks phonetically confusing marks (e.g., 'Xylo' vs 'Zilo')</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>3. Visual / Vienna</strong></td>
                  <td>Figurative code classifications</td>
                  <td>Identifies similar device emblems and logo graphics</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>4. Well-Known Marks</strong></td>
                  <td>Cross-class protection lists</td>
                  <td>Protects famous brands even outside their primary classes</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2>3. Section 9 vs Section 11 Objections</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Section 9 (Absolute Grounds):</strong> Is the name too generic, descriptive, or devoid of distinctiveness? Example: attempting to register "Organic Spices" for spice manufacturing will face an immediate Section 9 refusal.</li>
            <li><strong>Section 11 (Relative Grounds):</strong> Does the mark resemble an earlier mark registered or pending for identical or similar goods/services, creating a likelihood of public confusion?</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>4. Recommendations for Coining Strong Names</h2>
          <p>To maximize search clearance and registration speed, strive for coined, invented words (like Rolex, Google, or Haier), arbitrary words with no commercial connection to your product (like Apple for computers), or suggestive words requiring cognitive deduction.</p>
        </article>

        <div class="cta-panel" style="margin-top: 48px;">
          <p class="eyebrow">Clear Your Name Early</p>
          <h2>Request a Preliminary Search from BRNDNUR.</h2>
          <p>We check the official IP India registry across all relevant phonetic permutations and provide an objective viability appraisal.</p>
          <div class="cta-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-gold" href="https://wa.me/919048188899?text=Hello%20BRNDNUR%2C%20please%20check%20my%20brand%20name%20clearance." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inquire on WhatsApp &rarr;</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/brand-name-search/">Brand Search Page</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
